.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":2,"open_issues":11,"watchers":23,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/225"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/joshyorko/rcc/pull/225"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/issues/225"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/issues/225/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/225/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/225/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/statuses/b24b29fffab4581456a313a240257d681ad744fd"}},"author_association":"OWNER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/224","id":4753529812,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPqaJu88AAAABG1Ub1A","html_url":"https://github.com/joshyorko/rcc/pull/224","diff_url":"https://github.com/joshyorko/rcc/pull/224.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/joshyorko/rcc/pull/224.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/issues/224","number":224,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(storage): add immutable objects and expected-parent head CAS","user":{"login":"joshyorko","id":54248591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MjQ4NTkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54248591?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko","html_url":"https://github.com/joshyorko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Scope\nRefs #118. Disjoint RCC-native object/head storage lane. All implementation is additive under artifactprovider; existing Provider, treeartifact capture/materialization, CLI, and dependency files are unchanged.\n\n- Immutable Put/Get/Head with bounded SHA-256/size validation, strong opaque revisions and same-byte idempotence.\n- Named heads use expected parent digest + revision, conditional writes, and fresh publication tokens for ABA protection.\n- Lost/5xx write responses trigger bounded read-only reconciliation, never blind mutation retry.\n- Single-PUT S3-compatible HTTP transport with injected signer, redirect refusal, exact readback, cancellation and staging cleanup.\n- Fresh RCC code informed by Camp concepts only. No Camp runtime dependency or copied source; inspected Camp source lacked a root license.\n\n## Verification\nTested code tree: 032a4b3ee3127865f8ce7662f9e84d62d210e550. Local reviewed commit 6573bb7291ba7fbeb393047baef6b05b1f43cbe3; connector-published commit has the identical full tree.\n\nGo 1.26.5 Linux amd64 on cloud overlayfs. Parent independently reran scripts/verify-object-storage.sh successfully:\n- artifactprovider tests: PASS (0.881 s)\n- artifactprovider race: PASS (3.609 s)\n- go vet: PASS\n- Windows amd64 package test compilation: PASS, compile-only\n- git diff --check: PASS\nIndependent exact-tree review found no concrete must-fix and reran TestS3Storage successfully. Tests cover immutable conflicts, malformed/truncated/corrupt responses, early Close, stale/ABA heads, concurrent CAS, superseded readback ambiguity, cancellation and bounded reconciliation. Additional environmentartifact/artifacttrust package tests passed.\n\n## Unresolved verification boundaries\n- Full go test ./... was blocked by an unchanged operations/credentials_test.go test making a real request to https://end with synthetic credentials. No full-suite pass claimed and blocked request was not bypassed.\n- Three unchanged buildcoord native sandbox tests fail because bwrap cannot create a NETLINK_ROUTE socket in this cloud VM (Operation not permitted).\n- No live AWS/MinIO/R2 certification. Signer injection is provided, not credential discovery or a SigV4 implementation.\n- 64 MiB single-PUT cap; no multipart, CLI/materializer integration, or native Windows execution proof.\n\n## Documentation receipt\nCanonical guidance: docs/object-storage.md and one RCC development routing entry. Durable learning: content digests and backend revisions are distinct; ambiguous writes require verified reconciliation and head publication tokens preserve ABA detection. Evidence: additive implementation, offline/race tests and rerunnable verification script. No stale guidance removed. Remaining uncertainty: live backend conditional-write and signing compatibility.\n\nNo merge/tag/release requested.\n\n## Current acceptance attribution\n\nAt head `32d51bd00852b003fd0d82050f5fd6d281f362d5`, lint, coverage, CodeQL, quality and binary build passed; Linux native acceptance failed at the JAT producer filename assertion before provider creation. The same failure is now reproduced at unchanged main `47a60ea`: Conda resolves Perl5.44.0, whose payload omits `B::Terse.3`, `B::Op_private.3` and `B::Showlex.3`. The verified Perl5.32.1 build retains those intentional colon-name sentinels. DCO fixture repair `1b91a601d039605e6308bc49af3843b1aa869bd5`, included in PR#227 head7911566, passed the full Linux JAT workflow without weakening file-count or hash checks.\n\nThis attributes the observed JAT blocker to the shared upstream fixture, rather than object-storage changes. It does not establish that this storage head passes with the repair. Refresh from accepted main after #227 and the Go1.26.9 security patch integrate, then require exact-head native CI. Live S3-compatible certification, signing integration and the other verification boundaries above remain open; this PR remains a draft, with no merge/tag/release acceptance.\n","created_at":"2026-10-06T02:57:14Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T21:00:08Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cd9fe3314761bcf95da7160c0676d26d023f7a33","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/224/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/224/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/issues/224/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joshyorko/rcc/statuses/32d51bd00852b003fd0d82050f5fd6d281f362d5","head":{"label":"joshyorko:feat/rcc-object-storage-cas","ref":"feat/rcc-object-storage-cas","sha":"32d51bd00852b003fd0d82050f5fd6d281f362d5","user":{"login":"joshyorko","id":54248591,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MjQ4NTkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54248591?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko","html_url":"https://github.com/joshyorko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joshyorko/subscriptions","organizations